# scry's out-of-bounds rule pack (CWE-787 writes, CWE-125 reads)
#
# Two `kind memory` rules name the analyses with `check`; `Scry.Bounds` supplies the
# evidence (allocation size, tainted index/length, dominating bound check). Keep this
# pack separate from default.scry so a bounds claim is an explicit opt-in:
#
#   scry taint FILE.c --rules lib/Scry/rules/oob.scry
#
# The analysis is a may-analysis over the points-to locations. It reports only when the
# allocation's cell count is statically known; an unknown size is a
# `scry/memory/unknown-memory` diagnostic, not a finding.

rule out-of-bounds-write
  kind memory
  severity error
  message An attacker-controlled index writes outside an allocation
  check out-of-bounds-write
end

rule out-of-bounds-read
  kind memory
  severity error
  message An attacker-controlled index reads outside an allocation
  check out-of-bounds-read
end

# The pack must trust the cap sanitisers it expects an author to use; scry's model table
# only treats a model sanitiser as a kill when the pack names it. This rule has no
# sources or sinks: it exists only so `clamp_len`/`checked_size`/`clamp_size` clean the
# length they return.
rule oob-trusted-cap
  kind taint
  severity note
  message A length capped by a trusted policy model
  sanitise clamp_len result
  sanitise checked_size result
  sanitise clamp_size result
end
